# Panel 262's R5 (lane land262, step 215a): panel 258's stop, which spec
# § 13 promises: where C jumps out of a signal handler whose signal
# interrupted this runtime's allocator, the program aborts at the jump,
# saying so, where this runtime saw the handler begin and the jump. The
# watchdog of defect 2873's case with its handler installed by `sigaction`,
# its alarm repeating every 200 microseconds, each `siglongjmp`ing out of a
# loop of C calling a Heroes function that only allocates, until one lands
# inside this runtime's allocator.
# MUST STOP, at the jump, in words naming the jump out of the allocator.
extern "a-watchdog-jumping-out-of-the-allocator.h"
    function wds_run(cb: (function(i64) -> i64)) -> i64

function work(n: i64) -> i64
    xs: [i64] @= []

    for i in range(from: 0, to: 64)
        xs @ xs.push(i + n)

    return len(xs)

function main()
    print("the watchdog starts")
    print("a million alarms and none inside the allocator: ", wds_run(cb: work))
